    "result_text": "The full suite passes \u2014 **36 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors**, including the new `Cp26Tests` and all existing telephone tests (`Cp02`, `Cp03`, `Cp08`).\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe spec requires validating the E.164 national-number length against its country code. I implemented this in the existing normalization step and reused the existing 400 path.\n\n**`NormalizeOwnerTelephone.java`** \u2014 after the telephone is assembled into E.164 digits and passes the existing 8\u201315 digit check, a new `requireNationalLength(...)` step enforces per-country rules:\n- country code `61` \u2192 national number must be exactly **9** digits\n- country code `1` \u2192 national number must be exactly **10** digits\n- any other country code (e.g. `+64`) carries no length rule and passes through\n\nA wrong length throws the existing checked `InvalidTelephoneException`, which its handler already maps to **400**. I updated the javadocs on both the function and the exception to document the new rule.\n\nThis keeps the OfficeFloor conventions intact \u2014 one function class, one public method, a checked escalation handled by the YAML-registered handler \u2014 and doesn't touch the pipeline wiring since the 400 vehicle already exists.",
